ely in summer when u started this).  My daughter was a 2025 who just started at a D2 in Florida.  For her - recruiting for d2/d3 picked up speed late spring of junior year.  She talked with schools all summer after junior year.  Did recruiting  trips in Sept/Oct Senior year.  Committed/signed after that. \n\nAlso - if u really like this school/team, I would still do the visit!  And just stop by the pool to see if you can say hi. That shows initiative.  One my my daughter’s final-four schools where she did an OV resulted from a random drive-through the school where she walked into the pool and met the coach.  Good luck","createdAt":"2025-10-02T15:18:00.000Z","replyCount":0,"reactionCount":4,"repliesCursor":"","author":{"name":"Dave Bell","platformUserId":"pfbid02GBDzq3VPru3jRk1AhprS7hzo6KRNRUWQaWiL3amCozKbhcS4LjXKvNZyb1Move4pl","shortName":"Dave"}},{"id":"Y29tbWVudDo3NzcxNTE1OTUzMDI4ODZfNzc3NzI4Nzk1MjQ1MTY2","text":"My daughter had to reach out 4 times before she got a response from her top choice school. Finally she wrote an email that said we will be in the area on these dates and I would love to meet you. She got a response right away and was shocked that the coach gave her 2 hours of her time!","createdAt":"2025-10-02T16:27:44.000Z","replyCount":0,"reactionCount":0,"repliesCursor":"","author":{"name":"Anonymous participant 533","platformUserId":"1718741588789416","shortName":null}},{"id":"Y29tbWVudDo3NzcxNTE1OTUzMDI4ODZfNzc3NjUyNzAxOTE5NDQy","text":"Many programs have tons of ‘26 recruits on visits currently so I’m guessing they are short on time. My daughter’s team is hosting 7 recruits this weekend as they still filling their roster for next year. Although it’s stressful stick with it-the timeline is fluid. Good luck! 🍀","createdAt":"2025-10-02T14:43:21.000Z","replyCount":0,"reactionCount":2,"repliesCursor":"","author":{"name":"Colleen Lai Taylor","platformUserId":"pfbid023bbKkFkDGHDy4Nc49j99FjPzkWuES2svif92mDNyo6fogdh4SZo6Fbk4rSrWyAXSl","shortName":"Colleen"}}